PROJECT-SPECIFIC GUIDANCE

This project has two codelines — mocka and mockb — both declaring a TypeScript-plus-vitest
stack. Both tickets in scope require editing TypeScript source files under src/ in those
codelines: MOCK3-1 touches src/fares.ts in mocka, and MOCK3-2 touches src/schedule.ts in mockb.

Three roles were minted. Two are investigators — mocka-fares-investigator and
mockb-schedule-investigator — whose briefs are to confirm a bug, its test gap, and its caller
blast radius before any fix is written. Investigators do not edit source files; their output is
a findings report, not a repository change. The third role, typescript-vitest-engineer, is the
sole implementer and spans both codelines: its brief is to author the logic fix in TypeScript
source under src/ in mocka and mockb.

This is the exact trap the Live 2026-08-07 warning describes. Every ticket here needs a code
change in a repository, so the role that owns the source files — not the role that investigates
them — is the one that can deliver. Assign accordingly.
